{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen","id":675454,"title":"Outcaste Dragonblooded Beastmen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T11:25:09-07:00","id":675454,"title":"Outcaste Dragonblooded Beastmen","content":"...Just a weird thought I suddenly had.<br /> I mean, it's been said that the Realm and Lookshy both are... well, not aggressively recruiting, but still very much willing to take in outcaste Dragonblooded, because more dragonblooded blood is always good. It also mentions somewhere that these recruited DBs are considered slightly &quot;less pure&quot; than &quot;proper&quot; Dynasts, but still far above any mortal.<br /> Would that still apply to Beastmen that exalt as Terrestrials?<br /> Or would the associations between Beastmen and barbarians and Lunar Anathema make that impossible?<br /> Or is it in-between: Yes, they get accepted into the Realm, but will be considered as &quot;Third-Rate Dragonblooded&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:33:59-07:00","id":675499,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Realm and Lookshy have a monolithic perspective on beastmen. I could see pious Immaculates railing an outcaste beastfolk as a degenerate heresy, and I could see an equally pious Immaculate arguing that the mere fact of his Exaltation is proof that he is no lower than any other Dragon-Blood. The general answer is probably gonna lie somewhere between those two extremes\u2014it's even easier to look down on and discriminate against people of lower social standing when they have patently bestial features, but at the same time, it would be very stupid indeed to let the opportunity to recruit an outcaste slip through your fingers just because they look funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T11:40:36-07:00","id":675551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675499#post675499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see pious Immaculates railing an outcaste beastfolk as a degenerate heresy, and I could see an equally pious Immaculate arguing that the mere fact of his Exaltation is proof that he is no lower than any other Dragon-Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>And because I just read the &quot;Ask the Developers&quot; topic summary, now I'm wondering: Which of the two would Peleps Deled kill?<br /> (Though I expect the answer to that would be &quot;Whatever the storyteller decides&quot;. Also, possibly, &quot;Both&quot;.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:40:52-07:00","id":675611,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the Beastman would be allowed into the Realm, but he would have to take the razor of the coin (most likely the razor), would generally be sneered at and treated rather poorly by the other Dragon Blooded (even other ex-Outcastes) and definitely wouldn't be allowed to marry into a Great House no matter what sort of victories or epic feats he managed to accomplish.. Even House Nellens, which is generally the most open towards recruiting Outcastes would probably view the social issues of openly adding a Beastmen to their House to outweigh any advantages, though maybe they would be willing to add him in under the fiction of recruiting him as of a mercenary. That's likely the absolute best that a beastman Terrestrial could hope to accomplish in the Realm. <br /> <br /> They could probably fair a little better in Lookshy, but I imagine overall a beastman Terrestrial would likely be happier to simply go his own way in the world, or try to join a smaller group (Eos and Oessa, the Forest Witches, Saloy Hins Legion) who would likely be more accepting and welcoming than to try and &quot;fit in&quot; in the Realm or Lookshy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T12:57:13-07:00","id":675618,"title":"","content":"It's gonna vary a lot from Dragonblooded to Dragonblooded. The idea that there will be any sort of unanimous bigotry against one particular kind or another is fairly absurd. After all, they managed to Exalt. That alone is worth a measure of respect, whatever you happen to look like.<br /> <br /> That said if these Beastfolk Princes of the Earth come from a hostile nation, say Dzibilchan there will probably be a lot more hostility on the side of the Realm Dragonblooded. Honestly as far as Outcastes are concerned, I'm more interested in the reaction of a Luthean DB to the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:01:58-07:00","id":675622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675618#post675618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly as far as Outcastes are concerned, I'm more interested in the reaction of a Luthean DB to the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outch. Awesome Sharkdaughter exalts as fire aspect. Not a nice image.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:13:24-07:00","id":675659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675622#post675622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outch. Awesome Sharkdaughter exalts as fire aspect. Not a nice image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is an Exalt that has been treated like anything but exalted, who's had sand kicked in their face for as far back as they can remember, called &quot;Traitorspawn&quot; and ostracized, oppressed. And then they end up in the Realm, where they are to be treated as Princes of the Earth. What sort of character comes of that kind of shift in treatment? From scorn to worship?<br /> <br /> Will they embrace the sort of abuse they suffered through now that they hold the stick, or will they show more compassion towards the poor and disenfranchised, recalling their time in such straits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 09-23-2015, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:19:46-07:00","id":675664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675622#post675622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outch. Awesome Sharkdaughter exalts as fire aspect. Not a nice image.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> O M G<br /> Now I REALLY Want this to be canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Please De.s, bring Back Sharkdaughter (older and Terrestial exalted) in EX3!<br /> <br /> Amakawa Yuuto, thanks for new personal headcanon (and now, my-game-canon ^^ )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:22:28-07:00","id":675666,"title":"","content":"Dean Shomshak wrote a society of alligator-people Dragon-Bloods with this exact issue in mind. The Lunar that created them anticipated that as beastmen there would naturally be more hostility on both sides and they would have little chance of being absorbed into the Realm.<br /> <br /> Of course this entire plan was a nightmarish disaster, but the thought was interesting. <br /> <br /> Also there is a snakeman Outcaste working out of Nexus, Oliphas Ses. Another is mentioned in the backstory of Seven Devil Clever, and I think there are a couple more among the Forest Witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:28:12-07:00","id":675670,"title":"","content":"I doubt that Luthe's society is going to remain intact for EX3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675666#post675666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dean Shomshak wrote a society of alligator-people Dragon-Bloods with this exact issue in mind. The Lunar that created them anticipated that as beastmen there would naturally be more hostility on both sides and they would have little chance of being absorbed into the Realm.<br /> <br /> Of course this entire plan was a nightmarish disaster, but the thought was interesting.<br /> <br /> Also there is a snakeman Outcaste working out of Nexus, Oliphas Ses. Another is mentioned in the backstory of Seven Devil Clever, and I think there are a couple more among the Forest Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to have mistaken SDC for Huyla, because Seven Devil Clever's nemesis was a regular outcaste Terrestrial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:30:26-07:00","id":675673,"title":"","content":"Mhmm, Dzibilchan, Holiday in Cambodia where the Khmer Rouge are part Crocodillia part Fireball slinging Demigods.<br /> <br /> Probably the most amusing part of any Realm conflict there is that both sides would refer to the other side as <i>animals</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T13:33:37-07:00","id":675677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675666#post675666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dean Shomshak wrote a society of alligator-people Dragon-Bloods with this exact issue in mind. The Lunar that created them anticipated that as beastmen there would naturally be more hostility on both sides and they would have little chance of being absorbed into the Realm.<br /> <br /> Of course this entire plan was a nightmarish disaster, but the thought was interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That whole thing was an infuriating mix of one of the best ideas I'd ever seen and some of the worst execution of why it didn't work in the whole gameline.<br /> <br /> It's like, yes. A whole society of Dragon-Blooded beastmen, hidden away in the jungle primeval of the deep southwest, painstakingly created by a Lunar Exalted. That's fucking pure gold is what it is, man. I can do so much with that.<br /> <br /> And the reason it didn't work is because Chejop Kejak personally walked down off his mountain and slapped the taste out of said Lunar's mouth in his completely inaccessible sanctum, which isn't so inaccessible at all because Kejak.<br /> <br /> That is the textbook example of <i>the precise wrong way to use Chejop Kejak. </i>That's not what he should be spending his time doing, and it is a head-deskingly awful way of utilizing high-essence, ancient Sidereals that plays right into the old and unfun stereotypes of &quot;but but but I can't ever get too successful or the Siddies will just throw some E8 baddass at me who'll punch my soul out, and they can find me anywhere and penetrate any defense.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:55:50-07:00","id":675726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675659#post675659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is an Exalt that has been treated like anything but exalted, who's had sand kicked in their face for as far back as they can remember, called &amp;quot;Traitorspawn&amp;quot; and ostracized, oppressed. And then they end up in the Realm, where they are to be treated as Princes of the Earth. What sort of character comes of that kind of shift in treatment? From scorn to worship?<br /> <br /> Will they embrace the sort of abuse they suffered through now that they hold the stick, or will they show more compassion towards the poor and disenfranchised, recalling their time in such straits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Lutheans Exalting too. I ramped up the cool though. A Traiterspawn Exalts as a Terrestrial. And when the mob came for her, a sibling, out of love and angry at the ipression and bigotry,stood up to defend her...and recieved a Zenith Exaltation for it.<br /> <br /> Even better, guess whos Exaltation he/she would recieve","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T14:58:10-07:00","id":675728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also mentions somewhere that these recruited DBs are considered slightly &quot;less pure&quot; than &quot;proper&quot; Dynasts, but still far above any mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div> On a slight tangent, I don't think this will be the case anymore. A fine child of Mnemon should be significantly above somebody who Exalted because a Dynast took a shine to their great-great-great grandmama. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it would be very stupid indeed to let the opportunity to recruit an outcaste slip through your fingers just because they look funny.</div> </div> </div> </div> I could picture that as a scenario in which a student of Pasiap's Stair wears heavy wraps all the time, claiming that it's a cultural thing or to cover up some scars or something. The latter might be more effective... I think Pasiap's Stair does a thing where they beat your prior cultural identity out of you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:18:31-07:00","id":675738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675728#post675728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On a slight tangent, I don't think this will be the case anymore. A fine child of Mnemon should be significantly above somebody who Exalted because a Dynast took a shine to their great-great-great grandmama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think this will change.<br /> Remember, there's a bit of doublethink going on here: Yes, the Realm knows breeding is a thing, but at the same time, the Immaculate Order preaches that those who exalted as Dragonblooded are <i>blessed by the Dragons</i> and their divine representatives in Creation, Princes of the Earth, while those who didn't exalt as Dragonblooded are mere mortals who must follow the guidance of those with the Blood of Dragons.<br /> A fine (mortal) child of Mnemon is <i>still</i> lower in the divine hierarchy than that outcaste Dragonblooded, for the sole reason that <i>it didn't exalt</i>. If the dragons wanted it to stand equal or above the outcaste Dragonblooded, they'd have graced it with their blessings.<br /> <br /> (Unless you meant &quot;A fine (exalted) child of Mnemon&quot; and just meant that the &quot;slightly less pure&quot; turned into &quot;a lot less pure&quot;. That might be more reasonable, but still, any DB is higher than any mortal - at least outside of house Nellens (that was the quasi-mortal house, right?).)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:24:55-07:00","id":675741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675677#post675677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That whole thing was an infuriating mix of one of the best ideas I'd ever seen and some of the worst execution of why it didn't work in the whole gameline.<br /> <br /> It's like, yes. A whole society of Dragon-Blooded beastmen, hidden away in the jungle primeval of the deep southwest, painstakingly created by a Lunar Exalted. That's fucking pure gold is what it is, man. I can do so much with that.<br /> <br /> And the reason it didn't work is because Chejop Kejak personally walked down off his mountain and slapped the taste out of said Lunar's mouth in his completely inaccessible sanctum, which isn't so inaccessible at all because Kejak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weeeell, it fell apart because Chejop disappeared, but he was only the final straw. The real problem was that the Lunar put no contingency plans in place for the society to function without him. And it was, of course, a nightmarish slave camp state. The Lunar was equally at fault for the collapse, and for the collapse being deserving. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T15:34:08-07:00","id":675746,"title":"","content":"I think a Beastperson Lost Egg who gets snapped up by the Realm isn't going to have the same razor or coin choice forced on them that a more human one would. What's more likely to happen is that some house or the immaculate order takes them and and trains them into some sort of agent who spends all of their time on the threshold. They will likely never marry because no Patrician house wants to risk their children coming out with fur and fangs and then having to wait 20 years in the hopes that there's enough exalted blood in them to exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:09:28-07:00","id":675828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675738#post675738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't think this will change.<br /> Remember, there's a bit of doublethink going on here: Yes, the Realm knows breeding is a thing, but at the same time, the Immaculate Order preaches that those who exalted as Dragonblooded are <i>blessed by the Dragons</i> and their divine representatives in Creation, Princes of the Earth, while those who didn't exalt as Dragonblooded are mere mortals who must follow the guidance of those with the Blood of Dragons.<br /> A fine (mortal) child of Mnemon is <i>still</i> lower in the divine hierarchy than that outcaste Dragonblooded, for the sole reason that <i>it didn't exalt</i>. If the dragons wanted it to stand equal or above the outcaste Dragonblooded, they'd have graced it with their blessings.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a huge difference between spiritual elevation and social standing. <br /> <br /> That mortal child of Mnemon will probably be invited to all the big parties and have lots of close friends and contacts among the movers and shakes of the Realm. That Outcast, while people will bow to him, won't be getting any invitations to major events and will largely be looked down on as a barbarian (socially) even by mortals. Until he manages to marry into one of the Houses, he'll always be an outsider in the Realm and many people will look down on him (socially) even if they grudgingly respect his spiritual enlightenment.<br /> <br /> In many situations it would be very apparent that the mortal, with her allies, contacts, family and money would functionally have much more power and influence and thereby receive more respect and be above a Dragon Blooded Outcast with no strong ties or powerful allies in the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T17:58:54-07:00","id":675855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675828#post675828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many situations it would be very apparent that the mortal, with her allies, contacts, family and money would functionally have much more power and influence and thereby receive more respect and be above a Dragon Blooded Outcast with no strong ties or powerful allies in the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems worth noting that the devs have said more than once that we'll actually get some wordcount for mortal Dynasts this edition.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting: it seems to me that &quot;as an outcaste, any sort of outcaste regardless of if you have hair and teeth or scales and fangs, you will in general be viewed as a kind of lesser outsider by most Dynasts, even those who might want to recruit you&quot; has always been baked into the Realm as part of Scarlet's social engineering design. The two big obvious &quot;OUTCASTES CAN ACHIEVE POWER AND INFLUENCE HERE&quot; signs point at the Immaculate Order and the Legions for a reason; every outcaste funneled there is one less Dragon-Blooded loyal to a Great House and one more loyal to either the state religion or the Empress personally. The Legions especially are going to be a big draw for older outcastes who have been making a go of it out in the Threshold or beyond for awhile, I think, as Dragon-Blooded are used to thinking of themselves as hard, bad dudes and it is generally known the Empress promotes on merit. You too could have a Dragonlord's baton in your knapsack!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T18:55:25-07:00","id":675903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675728#post675728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could picture that as a scenario in which a student of Pasiap's Stair wears heavy wraps all the time, claiming that it's a cultural thing or to cover up some scars or something. The latter might be more effective... I think Pasiap's Stair does a thing where they beat your prior cultural identity out of you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just wear a basket on your head.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://soul-society.weebly.com/uploads/3/3/3/0/333061/6635647.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:06:26-07:00","id":675940,"title":"","content":"That's a <i>tengai</i>, one of the best hats known to man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T19:16:16-07:00","id":675946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675666#post675666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there is a snakeman Outcaste working out of Nexus, Oliphas Ses.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not an outcaste, he's a Night Caste Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T20:13:07-07:00","id":675981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675726#post675726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Lutheans Exalting too. I ramped up the cool though. A Traiterspawn Exalts as a Terrestrial. And when the mob came for her, a sibling, out of love and angry at the ipression and bigotry,stood up to defend her...and recieved a Zenith Exaltation for it.<br /> <br /> Even better, guess whos Exaltation he/she would recieve</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of my standing character ideas, actually, though without the twist of having a DB sibling.<br /> <br /> Gavrane Anyala's brother was just going to be sacrificed, so - like the fair-minded eight-year-old she was - she crawled through a set of vents too small for any adult and went to go tell Leviathan that he was a <i>meanie</i>.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, her Exaltation had <i>really</i> good timing. Even more fortunately, feeling his Bond go bingbingbing at the little girl with 'Traitor' <i>backlit by her caste mark</i> was enough to give him a 'What Have I Done'? moment about her circumstances, so he treated her like a mentor figure rather than... Well, Amyana directly returned, or Just Another Traitorspawn.<br /> <br /> OTOH, having <i>Freaking Leviathan</i> for a mentor for six or more years does not produce a balanced starting PC, especially when they're sitting on a treasure trove of first age stuff like Luthe, so I've never had any expectation of actually getting to play her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T23:16:58-07:00","id":676088,"title":"","content":"Not sure if the rhythm is quite perfect, but the thread title almost fits <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/1412/\" target=\"_blank\">this xkcd</a>.<br /> <br /> Warning: you can't stop noticing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T02:26:09-07:00","id":676217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675738#post675738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, there's a bit of doublethink going on here: Yes, the Realm knows breeding is a thing, but at the same time, the Immaculate Order preaches that those who exalted as Dragonblooded are <i>blessed by the Dragons</i> and their divine representatives in Creation, Princes of the Earth, while those who didn't exalt as Dragonblooded are mere mortals who must follow the guidance of those with the Blood of Dragons.<br /> A fine (mortal) child of Mnemon is <i>still</i> lower in the divine hierarchy than that outcaste Dragonblooded, for the sole reason that <i>it didn't exalt</i>. If the dragons wanted it to stand equal or above the outcaste Dragonblooded, they'd have graced it with their blessings.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Were you not talking about breeding? You said &quot;more blood is good&quot;, it looked a lot like you were talking about breeding. &quot;Hey, this rube from the Threshold is a far better breeding match than the child of two Exalted who themselves have numerous Exalted relatives going back five generations&quot; is what I thought you were going for.<br /> <br /> Although even then... look at what outcastes actually get used for. You may be considered more spiritually refined, but you're not really living like a Prince of the Earth. The mortal children of Dynasts are almost certainly going to live in greater luxury than you, especially when their marriage to another well-bred mortal yields the fruit of about four or five Exalted children.<br /> <br /> How many Exalted children is your beastfolk outcaste going to have? One? If they're lucky, and have a fairly well-bred partner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T03:01:45-07:00","id":676253,"title":"","content":"There's also the matter of the Outcastes in the Immaculate Order.<br /> <br /> Assuming about half go in\u200bto the Order and half go into the Legions, this implies that the Empress had a deliberate strategy of making it difficult for Outcastes to breed. After all, half of them are banned from doing so. This implies she doesn't want too large a group of Outcastes in the Realm: the Empire may want more Dragonblood, but Scarlet is/was a matriarch, and perhaps wanted to ensure that her family stayed at the top, while those unrelated to her got sent to do the dangerous jobs that require a lot of Dragonblooded, but don't necessarily give them a ton of power or resources.<br /> <br /> Of course, now it's 768 years since she founded the thing, she may feel little connection with her great(x10) grand-kids, and they likely feel little familial connection to her, but only to their House. But I imagine this idea has bled into Realm culture: you'd rather marry a member of the dynasty than some foreigner. Does this contradict the Immaculate Philosophy? Yes, but people do things that contradict their own religion all the time.<br /> <br /> There's probably something about foreigners vs Realm natives too. If a peasant exalts as a Dragonblood, a few days later the Dynast who owns the land turns up and while the peasants grovel before her announces thats he's finally found the long-lost grand-son of his dead brother, and in his honour she wants to adopt this &quot;lost egg&quot; as her son (of course, he'll never be fully accepted as he's an ill-mannered boor, but the House will grab him nonetheless). Whereas if a Medoan janissary exalts while on campaign for the Realm, no-one's letting him join their House, it's the coin or the razor for him.<br /> <br /> (Plus, chances are said Exalted peasant <i>is</i> the great-great-great-great-great-grandson of the Empress, because half the Blessed Isle are. Whereas the Medoan jannisary probably isn't.)<br /> <br /> Now, a beastman has all of these issues at the same time. It's a monstrous freak, an abomination against the Immaculate Philosophy by its very nature, but it's also a Dragonblood. Honestly, knowing the prejudice against them (if they don't know already, they'll probably find out quickly), few Beastmen are likely to go to the Realm, they'd rather rule a Beastman tribe. But if they did... I imagine that they'll be told to take the Razor or Coin, and then have an &quot;accident&quot; in training (if you read the fluff, this happens more than you'd think for valuable super-soldiers, because disloyal super-soldiers are a big risk).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T03:22:58-07:00","id":676262,"title":"","content":"I've got this image now in which a marginal bit of theology is the idea that a beastfolk who Exalts is being given the opportunity to redeem the indiscretions of their ancestor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676253#post676253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Empire may want more Dragonblood</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially, but balanced against concerns of stability and control. The Immaculate Order is part of the apparatus for limiting the number of Dynasts as well.<br /> <br /> Although with the way I see Terrestrial inheritance, limiting the opportunities of outcastes actually serves the purpose of preventing them to do anything that would actually <i>reduce</i> the number of Dynasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T03:42:17-07:00","id":676274,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Imperial Beastman of 2nd ed 40K! Go forth and redeem your filthy sin of existing by fighting for the Imperium!<br /> <br /> But yes, that was (well, partially) my point. They don't exactly want more Dragonblood: they want more loyal, competent, sane Dragonblood who fulfil society's expectations of them. If it was just about the number of Dragonblood, they'd just set up huge harems, but having tons of super-soldiers in your country is not always a good thing.<br /> Beastmen do not fulfil what the Realm wants from Dragonblood. They're theologically awkward, and hardly inspire loyalty or devotion. Nor can you expect them to be very loyal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T04:20:40-07:00","id":676289,"title":"","content":"Would a society of reptilian beastman DBs step on the Dragon Kings' toes somewhat? Or would the two be different enough to avoid much overlap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T04:24:10-07:00","id":676291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676289#post676289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or would the two be different enough to avoid much overlap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely they should be. I mean, the implications of reincarnation and life stages alone...<br /> <br /> I mean, when it all comes down to it, Dragon Kings are basically magic dinosaurs rather than reptile looking humans. Even small things like picturing the differences in the body plans can get it across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T04:25:52-07:00","id":676295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676217#post676217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were you not talking about breeding? You said &quot;more blood is good&quot;, it looked a lot like you were talking about breeding. &quot;Hey, this rube from the Threshold is a far better breeding match than the child of two Exalted who themselves have numerous Exalted relatives going back five generations&quot; is what I thought you were going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;More blood is good&quot; is just the general reasoning as for why the Realm and Lookshy want <i>all the DBs</i>. If someone else has a bigger Dragonblooded population then they have, they're going to have some trouble maintaining their positions of power.<br /> That's unrelated (kinda) to their social hierarchy of &quot;DBs &gt; Mortals&quot;, which I was more concerned about. The Realm draws its entire legitimacy from &quot;DB &gt; Mortals&quot;, so I don't see that principle shifting - it's kind of a core concept of them. Sure, the mortal Dynast may have a higher breeding than that Lost Egg that <i>literally</i> hatched in the threshold, and that's going to be reflected in any political intermarriages, but at the same time, a former outcaste has <i>still</i>, officially, in a higher social status than that mortal Dynast. Hence, doublethink. &quot;Yes, the honorable Bird-Who-Hatched is graced by the Dragons and obviously a better marriage partner than any mortal. I'm still going to marry my child to Mnemon Mortal Jr., because, y'know, reasons.&quot;<br /> What I was asking about is how the different weights on that scale - &quot;DBs are holier than thou&quot; vs. &quot;Beastmen are tainted savage pawn of the Lunar Anathema&quot; would play out.<br /> <br /> Sending him to the Legions or the Immaculate Order seems about right. It's still an &quot;officially honorable&quot; choice, while still keeping him out of actual High Society.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T05:00:08-07:00","id":676310,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's rare enough that there's no official word on it, and if it comes up in your game, a lot of monks spend a lot of time arguing.<br /> <br /> <br /> It did come up in our game: we visited one of our PCs' family, and met her father, Cynis Belar Rus, a very dodgy man. Some of the PCs discovered his terrible secret: a Dragonblooded man-bat living in a tower, a member of the family. Cue a lot of punching and then everyone refusing to talk about it, but being very suspicious of each other, with feuds that continued but none of those involved would admit what the feud was about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:25:26-07:00","id":676344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676253#post676253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. But if they did... I imagine that they'll be told to take the Razor or Coin, and then have an &quot;accident&quot; in training (if you read the fluff, this happens more than you'd think for valuable super-soldiers, because disloyal super-soldiers are a big risk).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... this thread has got me thinking about it, and do we actually have any good information on what happens to <i>adult</i> outcastes who either decide or are forced to go to the Realm?<br /> <br /> Because the Realm's entire training structure for outcastes, as presented in 1e and 2e, seems enormously structured around what to do with <i>young</i>, <i>internal</i> outcastes, people like Kasif who are peasants (or worse) with no connection to a Great House who pop during adolescence, like Dragon-Blooded do. Pasiap's Stair, much like the other secondary schools, is a school for children. The Realm is probably not dumb enough to attempt to force experienced adult Exalts into a training program populated by and designed for children and adolescents. That's a recipe for disaster and wastage.<br /> <br /> I have a hard time seeing a thirty-year-old Dragon-Blooded who has been tooling around beyond the Threshold for fifteen years and has mastered a whole bunch of Charms and maybe even has his own daiklave being sent to Pasiap's, or really anywhere, for &quot;training.&quot; That guy is going to be a special case, because there aren't going to be all that many of him.<br /> <br /> What I imagine happens is that Great Houses will make him an offer if they think he's worth something to them. Guy clearly has a lot of potential; he's survived a decade and a half out in the barbarous hinterlands with no formal training and has even managed to master his essence and unlock its secrets to a certain degree. He has whatever skills he's managed to accrue, and his all-important Exaltation. They have wealth and power and the ability to offer him a much better life in general with lower risk than he'd have in the Threshold. He won't be his own master, but being your own master is risky; carving out a vest-pocket kingdom seems like a great idea until you realize you have to actually <i>run it</i>. So they're like &quot;hey, we can offer you specialized training in the form of actual sifus, and you'll live in this big mansion and have servants and slaves and a lot of jade to buy what strikes your fancy. This will be your yearly stipend. Yes, that <i>is</i> a lot of zeroes. All we ask in return is that you apply your talents in the way we direct.&quot;<br /> <br /> (The Great Houses may neglect to mention the fact that this guy will need a lot of remediation in order to be socially acceptable at mixed-group formal gatherings and that people will constantly make fun of his High Realm accent and he's not allowed to murder them, and that the odds of a good marriage or rising above entry level in the House's hierarchy of Dragon-Blooded are very low.)<br /> <br /> The Legions and the Order will probably make their own pitch. I can't imagine the Order will have a very strong one, but the Legion one will probably be along the lines of &quot;you'll work your ass off, but unlike the Houses if you survive and thrive we'll promote you and give you power and authority. Imagine ten thousand soldiers marching to your whim. You won't get <i>that</i> doing the dirty work of House Sesus; all you'll get is a pat on the head and maybe the snide remarks about your birth status will slack off... for awhile.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:40:11-07:00","id":676349,"title":"","content":"I've considered this before, as it's come up in games. I think, to be fair, Pasiap's Stair and the Cloister probably do work well for youths, as well as children, but there is the point about, say, a powerful Dragonblood adventurer, or the Dragonblooded king of a small country.<br /> <br /> My guess is that, firstly\u200b, these are the sorts of Dragonblood who are slightly less likely to want to go to the Realm (they're already doing well), but since there's still likely some who think this way, the Realm probably would prefer to do something like employ them as mercenaries or rulers of Threshold states.<br /> However, it is mentioned that a few houses have started aggressively adopting Outcastes (Tepet and V'neef). I'd guess this is the kind of outcaste they're talking about (peasants and patricians who exalt already get adopted). So if you're an experienced Dragonblood adventurer from, say, the Neck, they'll marry you to a mortal dynast from a weaker part of the family, and give you a job in the House Legion, where you're less likely to make some terrible social faux-pas.<br /> <br /> This implies that the oth\u200ber houses don't put so much effort into doing so.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if you're a sorcerer, Nellens will beg you to marry a Nellens and join the house. Nellens just love sorcerers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-24-2015, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T06:41:37-07:00","id":676350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676344#post676344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">([...] and that the odds of a good marriage [...] are very low.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Low for a good marriage by realm-standards. This is the perfect person to marry off to some rich mortal for money*. The mortal family manages to marry into a House, the House gets money, the outcaste gets a partner who, by threshold-standards, could still easily be considered a prince(ss).<br /> And hey, given their different lifespans, you can do so several times!<br /> <br /> ...the bigger problem would probably be &quot;There's a good chance that the House will want to decide on who you marry. If you have any other preferences, keep them secret.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> *: Rich merchants marrying into nobility is such a classic concept that I refuse to believe it doesn't happen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 09-24-2015, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:15:16-07:00","id":676364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676349#post676349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've considered this before, as it's come up in games. I think, to be fair, Pasiap's Stair and the Cloister probably do work well for youths, as well as children, but there is the point about, say, a powerful Dragonblood adventurer, or the Dragonblooded king of a small country.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't even need to be a powerful Dragon-Blooded adventurer, really. (Inasmuch as all the Exalted are powerful.) You could just be an &quot;average&quot; Dragon-Blooded adventurer who for one reason or another has managed to survive fifteen, twenty, thirty years before the option to go to the Realm, center of Dragon-Blooded culture and dwelling place of the Princes of the Earth, presents itself. We talk about &quot;going to the Realm&quot; but Creation is a huge place and for a lot of folks &quot;going to the Realm&quot; is going to entail a long costly journey through strange countries full of people whose languages they do not speak and whose customs they do not know. They will eventually, if they live long enough, gain the experience and competence to make that sort of trip... but that might take a long time. They might spend years stumbling through unlocking the secrets of their essence, learning the mysteries of its application through trial and error and insight. Many of them will live and die without ever going to the Threshold, much less the Realm... but some of them will travel around a bunch and decide they don't like the choices offered to them, and the Realm is overflowing with wealth and culture and toys and suchly.<br /> <br /> But by that point they're not going to be suitable for the Realm's secondary education institutions for a lot of reasons. It would be like sending someone in their thirties who'd had a semi-successful career to a high school; a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*: Rich merchants marrying into nobility is such a classic concept that I refuse to believe it doesn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly a thing, although if I recall correctly it is rare in the Realm for you to go more than one &quot;level&quot; up. Remember, your social position in the Realm isn't just an informal marker of status and power; it's a legal status in many regards. &quot;Peasant&quot; and &quot;Patrician&quot; and &quot;Dynast&quot; are terms that actually have legal, formal meanings and rights, duties, and privileges assigned to them. There are some wealthy peasants who are merchants; their ultimate endgame goal is to marry up into the patrician class. There are some wealthy, successful patrician clans; <i>their</i> ultimate endgame goal is to marry Dynasts. It's unusual to skip a step; you'd have to be a truly, disgustingly wealthy peasant-class merchant who for some odd reason had been unable to secure admittance to the patrician class yet and a Dynast would have to have truly desperate money needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:19:54-07:00","id":676365,"title":"","content":"Oh, rich patrician families absolutely look for impoverished Dragonblood to marry their kids to. It's just that most Dragonblood are too proud to do it, and can probably marry a mortal dynast. For an outcaste, however, it might be much more appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T07:34:28-07:00","id":676372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=675946#post675946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's not an outcaste, he's a Night Caste Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I must have gotten him mixed up with the other Exalted snake gangster from Seven Devil Clever's backstory. <br /> <br /> Also after refreshing my memory, the Forest Witches I was thinking of are not beast people. The Numina are something much weirder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T08:46:31-07:00","id":676430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676372#post676372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, I must have gotten him mixed up with the other Exalted snake gangster from Seven Devil Clever's backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no part of the description of her history in the core book that suggests Lombra Garua was one of the snakefolk. It only says that he was a gangster who had ruled her neighborhood for decades before she killed him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T09:54:45-07:00","id":676516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676430#post676430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no part of the description of her history in the core book that suggests Lombra Garua was one of the snakefolk. It only says that he was a gangster who had ruled her neighborhood for decades before she killed him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, I guess I'm just wrong about everything today. I'm sure I remember a DB Snakeman gangster <i>somewhere, </i>but I can't remember where.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T13:47:48-07:00","id":676845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676291#post676291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh absolutely they should be. I mean, the implications of reincarnation and life stages alone...<br /> <br /> I mean, when it all comes down to it, Dragon Kings are basically magic dinosaurs rather than reptile looking humans. Even small things like picturing the differences in the body plans can get it across.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, good. Because a while back I created a race if Dragon men based on ghe Drgonborn of D&amp;D 4. And made them the decendants of s First Age Gens whs Soar oatron wanted hus Dragon Bloided to be tual dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:52:46-07:00","id":676874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676516#post676516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welp, I guess I'm just wrong about everything today. I'm sure I remember a DB Snakeman gangster <i>somewhere, </i>but I can't remember where.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only official beastmen Dragon Blooded I can think of off hand were a race of bat-men in the East who kidnapped people to sacrifice to the sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:15:03-07:00","id":676885,"title":"","content":"I quite like Outcaste Beastman Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I think it's important though to keep the image behind them that they are fundamentally in the same class as the Dragonblooded, as essentially elemental harmony fueled enlightened warriors, who resonate with one another, and in some senses the lowest and scrappiest of the Exalted, who in the world of the Second Age hold themselves with a nobility, knowing their status in the world.<br /> <br /> You don't want them to fall into that image where they're just beastmen with an excuse to have some quirky elemental powers, and are not really Exalted of the Dragons, in any sense.<br /> <br /> I think Dynasty might have the same attitude in part at least. It is in how they are in Essence - how they hold themselves and how they act as Dragonblooded and take part in the mythos the Dynasty gives the Dragonblooded, that would in part determine their acceptance. If you are an Elemental Samurai Warrior who has a reptilian aspect to your features, then that you fulfil the Dynasty's standards of deportment and attitude and spirituality is a higher standard.<br /> <br /> If you are some debased creature that fulfills none of the Dynasty's standards for what a Dragonblood ought to be, without consciousness of yourself as Chosen of the Dragons, yet unaccountably has somehow stolen the power to use the might of the Dragons, then you are obviously a form of heresy and perhaps anathema.<br /> <br /> Remember, these people are *not* self consciously human; they regard themselves as something quite different due to an inner essence which they absolutely are discerning towards beyond mere appearances (and which many of the accoutrements of Dragonblooded power, Charms, aspect and anima, is perhaps only part).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T16:04:32-07:00","id":676937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676088#post676088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if the rhythm is quite perfect, but the thread title almost fits <a href=\"https://xkcd.com/1412/\" target=\"_blank\">this xkcd</a>.<br /> <br /> Warning: you can't stop noticing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You complete and utter <i>jerk</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T19:01:48-07:00","id":677124,"title":"","content":"No, sorry Aretii, that doesn' really fit :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T20:03:54-07:00","id":677189,"title":"","content":"OUTcaste DRAgon BLOODed BEASTmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T21:08:06-07:00","id":677210,"title":"","content":"From what I can tell, that beastman kingdom Dean Shomshak wrote (<a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\">Dzibilchan, Kingdom of the Crocodile)</a>, only existed on the old forums and did not survive the archive. Did anyone keep a copy and can it be shared?<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind; found it. See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/332532-dzibilchan-empire-of-the-alligator-dean-shomshak\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-25-2015, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T21:28:37-07:00","id":677216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=676937#post676937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You complete and utter <i>jerk</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. It only gets worse.<br /> <br /> <i>Silent Words of Dreams and Nightmares </i>is basically ruined for me. I even giggle when my phone tells me to take the <i>I-5 South toward San Diego.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T02:00:03-07:00","id":677428,"title":"","content":"Raph is the temperamental fire aspect, Don is the curious loremaster air aspect, Mikey is the zest for life wood aspect, Leo is the adaptable naturally gifted water aspect leader and splinter is the old traditionalist earth aspect. They're outcast and considered freaks by the people of the Imperial City, but they love that town and nightly purge it of crime and corruption.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:fixed Leo's aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 09-25-2015, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T06:08:37-07:00","id":677541,"title":"","content":"You left out Leo's Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T06:18:02-07:00","id":677543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=677541#post677541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You left out Leo's Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Water, due to being the only one left and the &quot;Adaptable&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T05:23:08-07:00","id":678920,"title":"","content":"I think a major factor with mutated Dragon-Blooded in the Realm is going to be how readily their mutations can be hidden away or bluffed as breeding marks. The &quot;petting zoo person&quot; beastfolk we normally see in the books have the worst deal there since it's difficult to conceal or downplay the entire shape of your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T06:27:15-07:00","id":678935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=678920#post678920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a major factor with mutated Dragon-Blooded in the Realm is going to be how readily their mutations can be hidden away or bluffed as breeding marks. The &quot;petting zoo person&quot; beastfolk we normally see in the books have the worst deal there since it's difficult to conceal or downplay the entire shape of your head.</div> </div> </div> </div>True - that said i find it extremely improbable any beastman that actually exalted as a terrestrial would seriously expect a positive welcome Realm considering how widespread distrust and prejudice is widespread among most civilized folk across Creation and the Realm is basically the nadir of civilization in the eyes of many in the Age of Sorrows. Too much risk and headache for a quite questionable gamble.<br /> <br /> Damn, i wouldn't put it above some wyld hunt groups or sworn brotherhoods across the Threshold killing any such outcastes as &quot;lunar anathema mocking the dragons&quot; or some equally self-serving excuse (to avoid any potential headaches involving relatives careless about their partner choices, among other things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T06:32:03-07:00","id":678939,"title":"","content":"They may also be quite likely to kill such outcastes as &quot;lunar anathema mocking the dragons&quot; because they actually think that's what's going on. They see a bestial monster with an anima banner... surely it must be an Anathema of some kind!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T07:58:18-07:00","id":679025,"title":"","content":"That's not how either the Immaculate Doctrine or Wyld Hunt Procedure works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T08:31:08-07:00","id":679053,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about the official Wyld Hunt, which has professional spies and Sidereal advisors working for it. I'm talking about the 3 or 4 local Dragonblood who hear of a powerful Exalted beast-lord and think &quot;sounds like an Anathema, it's our job to kill it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not to say that it isn't impossible that the masters of the Wyld Hunt might decide an influential or powerful beast-Dragonblood ought to be branded Anathema and slain, as he's probably an agent of those filthy beastman-spawning Lunars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-26-2015, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T09:09:11-07:00","id":679102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679053#post679053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about the official Wyld Hunt, which has professional spies and Sidereal advisors working for it. I'm talking about the 3 or 4 local Dragonblood who hear of a powerful Exalted beast-lord and think &quot;sounds like an Anathema, it's our job to kill it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>HEY GUYS!<br /> <img src=\"http://extras.mnginteractive.com/live/media/site138/2012/0713/20120713_054315_120712%20man%20on%20fire_300.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> A VILE ANATHEMA!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T10:22:10-07:00","id":679159,"title":"","content":"I suppose somebody who's really <i>really</i> ignorant might think that a Terrestrial beastfolk is some kind of Lunar. I can see there being a general prejudice against beastfolk that associates them with Lunars and Fair Folk, but I'd be highly dubious of the idea that this is extended to &quot;any Exalted beast person must be the pawn of an Anathema and we must kill them!&quot;, unless it's by an extremely zealous and poorly educated Realm person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T11:37:06-07:00","id":679202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679102#post679102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HEY GUYS!<br /> <img src=\"http://extras.mnginteractive.com/live/media/site138/2012/0713/20120713_054315_120712%20man%20on%20fire_300.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> A VILE ANATHEMA!</div> </div> </div> </div>HUUUUUUUUUUUUGS!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T11:59:37-07:00","id":679232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679053#post679053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about the official Wyld Hunt, which has professional spies and Sidereal advisors working for it. I'm talking about the 3 or 4 local Dragonblood who hear of a powerful Exalted beast-lord and think &quot;sounds like an Anathema, it's our job to kill it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not to say that it isn't impossible that the masters of the Wyld Hunt might decide an influential or powerful beast-Dragonblood ought to be branded Anathema and slain, as he's probably an agent of those filthy beastman-spawning Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree. What it really comes down to is the local cultures attitudes towards beastmen. <br /> <br /> For the most part in Creation, relations between humans and beastmen tend to be pretty negative. Beastmen are often viewed as pawns of Lunars or Fair Folk and find themselves at war with normal humans, and regions in which beastmen and human live peacefully tend to be extremely rare. While from an out-of-game perspective we know otherwise, many places and people don't even consider beastmen to be human but rather view them as distinctly inhuman monsters.<br /> <br /> If some beastman in Halta Exalted as a Terrestrial people there likely wouldn't care too much or treat him as any different from a normal human who Exalted as a Terrestrial. But in some places a Terrestrial beastman is simply going to be viewed as even more dangerous and monstrous than normal and the local Dragon Blooded will declare it to be Anathema (outside of the Realm/Lookshy that's often a code word for &quot;something we don't like and want to kill,&quot;) and go hunt it down because it <i>obviously</i> poses a danger to everyone, especially in regions with a more antagonistic relationship towards beastmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T14:39:45-07:00","id":679343,"title":"","content":"Wouldnt the attitude depend on the breed? From what I've seen, some are more accepted than others. Wolfmen, for example, are generally feared while Elkmen are usually seen as friendly neighbors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:16:27-07:00","id":679425,"title":"","content":"I think a local culture's attitudes towards a beastman will tend to trump more generalized attitudes.<br /> <br /> Hawkmen for example are accepted and welcomed in Halta, but in places that have suffered recent raids from the hawkmen of Mount Metagalapa, they'll probably view a Haltan Hawkmen as an enemy, even if the guy says, &quot;Honestly, I don't know anything about those Metagalapans!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Linnowan are probably going to be fairly hostile towards <i>all</i> beastmen, due in part to their longstanding war with Halta (which has fairly close relations to beastmen) as well as the fact that Linnowan is so close to the Realm which tends to frown on beastmen as well.<br /> <br /> Just because a breed is accepted in one place doesn't necessarily mean that it's accepted everywhere. It's also important to remember that most people in Creation tend to have negative attitudes and stereotypes towards beastmen, viewing them primarily as dangerous monsters rather than fellow humans. So while you may have local level interactions they will still be often colored by, &quot;Well this beatman (or tribe) is okay, but most of the rest of them are really dangerous,&quot; and the idea that civilized beastmen tend to be viewed as an exception rather than the rule.<br /> <br /> Places like Nexus or Halta, where beastmen are fully accepted and judged by what they do rather than by what they look like, tend to be comparatively rare in Creation. Even in An-Teng, which has a large colony of snakemen, they tend to be viewed as bizarre and strange and usually keep to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:58:07-07:00","id":679467,"title":"","content":"I think there's a far cry between a place being pragmatically cosmopolitan and fully accepting. Nexus in particular seems like the kind of place in which flare-ups of civil unrest would be relatively common, and beastfolk seem like they would be among the more common targets of such. All you need is one little scuffle between neighbourhoods, or for a child's body to show up with what some people insist are fang marks, and that supposedly accepted community of serpent folk can find themselves served up a nice little portion of tenderloin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:16:08-07:00","id":679474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679467#post679467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a far cry between a place being pragmatically cosmopolitan and fully accepting. Nexus in particular seems like the kind of place in which flare-ups of civil unrest would be relatively common, and beastfolk seem like they would be among the more common targets of such. All you need is one little scuffle between neighbourhoods, or for a child's body to show up with what some people insist are fang marks, and that supposedly accepted community of serpent folk can find themselves served up a nice little portion of tenderloin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd totally play a game where the LA riots happened in Nexus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:19:17-07:00","id":679475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679159#post679159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose somebody who's really <i>really</i> ignorant might think that a Terrestrial beastfolk is some kind of Lunar. I can see there being a general prejudice against beastfolk that associates them with Lunars and Fair Folk, but I'd be highly dubious of the idea that this is extended to &quot;any Exalted beast person must be the pawn of an Anathema and we must kill them!&quot;, unless it's by an extremely zealous and poorly educated Realm person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because there are no artifacts, hearthstones and strange magics that an &quot;enemy of Creation&quot; might use to make their anima appear like that of the dragon-blooded. Nor a lot of prejucide and suspicion against beastmen and the mutated, something compounded by the appearance of a number of lunars, across a considerable part of most urban societies in Creation and specially in the Threshold. Not to mention bigotry is a non-existant phenomena among the educated either....<br /> <br /> Yes, it will certainly vary from place to place, but honestly i'm not really seeing the Realm or the Dynasty as ones tending toward tolerant range of the spectrum, not by a long shoot. Normal-seeming outcastes that just look a lot like some uncle or another can be embarassing enough on itself, and while one with minor - and somewhat disguisable mutations might be acceptable for the sake of making the most of its potential, beastmen might be a little too much for many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-26-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T17:51:05-07:00","id":679487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679467#post679467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a far cry between a place being pragmatically cosmopolitan and fully accepting. Nexus in particular seems like the kind of place in which flare-ups of civil unrest would be relatively common, and beastfolk seem like they would be among the more common targets of such. All you need is one little scuffle between neighbourhoods, or for a child's body to show up with what some people insist are fang marks, and that supposedly accepted community of serpent folk can find themselves served up a nice little portion of tenderloin.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you're probably not going to find a place more accepting of beastmen in Creation than Nexus, where people will look at you for actions (and your coin purse) rather than your physical appearance. Even in Halta the local beastman tribes are held this weird, distant regard and nobody gets too close to them. Really, Beastmen are probably discriminated less in Nexus because of their race than anywhere else in Creation, and when a beastmen does face major discrimination in Nexus it's going to be because they're <i>poor</i> and the quality of life for a poor beastman won't be all that much different from all the rest of the poor people starving to death on the streets of the city.<br /> <br /> So I would say that of major metropolitan cities in Creation, Nexus is probably the most fully accepting of beastmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T18:16:45-07:00","id":679497,"title":"","content":"Here is what I think the general reactions would be:<br /> <br /> In The West:<br /> &quot;Ah, Sharkfolk Dragon-Blooded you say? Is it ok? Depends, is it Sharkman or Sharkwoman? Sharkman probably good for sailing, Sharkwoman not good.&quot;<br /> <br /> In The North:<br /> &quot;Hm, I probably won't trust him much, but we need all the power we can get to fight against the Bull In The North, as well as raids. Hire him as a merc.&quot;<br /> <br /> In The East:<br /> &quot;Hey, you Exalted, congratulations, we'll need power like that against those Realm Dragon-Bloods.&quot;<br /> <br /> In The Scavenger Lands:<br /> &quot;Look, they're all powerful dangerous people in the end, treat them with respect and fear like all the others....&quot;<br /> <br /> In The South:<br /> &quot;I don't care if they're Beastman, are they Water Aspect? Cause seriously, I'm thirsty and I don't care if I have to get them to shoot water right into my mouth....&quot;<br /> <br /> The Realm:<br /> &quot;It is not the place of a humble priest of the Immaculate Dragons such as I to judge whom they Exalt. Their choice is clear, this Beastman is above mortal men and therefore has all the rights of any Prince of Earth. Doesn't mean the rest of the Dragon-Blooded themselves should accept him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lookshy:<br /> &quot;Oh your a Dragon-Blooded too? We would like to offer you a place amongst us, you''ll be given a great education, weapons befitting your station, a purpose, and to live with your real peers. Don't expect to marry into any Gentes though.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Guild:<br /> &quot;Might I interest you with these high quality combs for all that fur you have, Prince of the Earth? Only ten obols!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T21:07:53-07:00","id":679636,"title":"","content":"Did i evermention the one idea I had for a group of Beadtman tribes. They were all founded by one lunar, and thetes twenty of them. A Bear one, A wolf one, 3 snake species, 2 Birds, Horse, Shark.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T07:49:39-07:00","id":680008,"title":"","content":"In a kind of unrelated but not quite note, just remembered how in Aspectbook: Air, Tepet Arada speaks of a period when he got pissed with his relatives constant and transparent goading of the house's youths in competing in valor &amp; heroism and left the Realm to live way up in the North for a few years, to meditate, trade furs with icewalkers and stuff. That and his return to family were a number of years before his now participation in the war against the Anathema Jochim, in RY 578-585.<br /> <br /> So it's perfectly possible for there to be some nearly centuries old bastard children of Arada or their descendants in some of the northern communities, or more ironically in hindsight, among the icewalkers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T08:18:00-07:00","id":680049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beastmen are probably discriminated less in Nexus because of their race than anywhere else in Creation</div> </div> </div> </div> What are you basing this on? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">when a beastmen does face major discrimination in Nexus it's going to be because they're poor</div> </div> </div> </div> Because there's never a disproportionate correlation between marginalized ethnic groups and poverty. I bet lots of beastfolk find it hard to find jobs or learn a respectable craft simply because there are always non-beastfolk with better qualifications, eh? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the quality of life for a poor beastman won't be all that much different from all the rest of the poor people starving to death on the streets of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div> Depends on all kinds of things, even as simple as their physical needs. Is there, say, a particular group that can only survive off of meat? It's going to be harder for them as a matter of course when money that buys meat for a day could buy grain for several weeks. Still, even focusing on the purely social stuff, does Nexus look like it's been written as the kind of Wretched Hive in which all of the poor people band together and do right by one another, universally and with no divisions? The place written in which city blocks regularly get into scuffles? A place which is a magnet for all kinds of people, including transients, from across the region, if not the world, coming in hoping to find a place in already limited space and resources? Oh yes, when a beastfolk community fleeing increasing raksha activities in the far East settles in Nexus, nobody is going to take their distinct and disturbing appearance and certain unusual customs as a cue to take out frustrations over increasing economic difficulty on them. No, Nexus is certainly written as that nice, inviting kind of virtual anarchy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T09:57:59-07:00","id":680093,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, in Nexus people are most typically discriminated against along economic lines rather than due to physical appearance. Whether you're a demon or a Raksha or a beastman, if you've got the coin to throw around, you'll find some level of acceptence in Nexus. In many other parts of Creation, that isn't going to be the case, and it won't matter how much money a beastman has, they'll always find themself being treated as a sub-human monster. And yes, a group of poor beastmen may face discrimination in Nexus depending on the current political headwinds, but it won't be all that different from what any group of poor people face.<br /> <br /> If there was an enclave of poor Great Forks ex-patriots, and then suddenly a huge number of refugees from Great Forks showed up, they too would face violence and such. Or would you suggest that that only happens to beastmen enclaves?<br /> <br /> The difference between the way way beastmen are treated in Nexus and beastman are treated elsewhere is that in Nexus, they aren't &quot;special&quot; (for good or ill) and aren't going to be viewed much differently from any other group of people, unless they have some particularly dangerous drawback like only being able to eat humans, or are particularly hideous. In the end, what matters the most in Nexus is how much money you have. And a rich beastman will be treated pretty much just like a rich human, and a poor beastman will be treated about the same as any poor human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-27-2015, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T11:55:20-07:00","id":680212,"title":"","content":"The problem is that there isn't just the binary divide of &quot;rich&quot; and &quot;poor&quot;. Once a person is suitably rich or poor, other people won't care whether he's a beastman, Fair Folk or whatever, sure. But in the spaces in-between, there can fit a lot of discrimination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T12:15:02-07:00","id":680244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=680093#post680093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, what matters the most in Nexus is how much money you have. And a rich beastman will be treated pretty much just like a rich human, and a poor beastman will be treated about the same as any poor human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being rich won't protect you from the racism of the rich, and being poor won't protect you from the racism of the poor.<br /> <br /> What's different about Nexus is that the locals are going to have a slightly higher tolerance for weirdness than, say, the people of the Imperial City; they won't freak out and think you're a subhuman monster come to eat their children, but they'll still assume that you are a barbarian, or sneaky, or violent, or (stereotype).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T12:49:14-07:00","id":680317,"title":"","content":"There's a middle ground between total acceptance and Wyld Hunt. In between lie many ugly shades of discrimination, and both overt and covert racism.<br /> <br /> And being a marginalized ethnic group does lead to more poverty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T12:57:44-07:00","id":680335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=680244#post680244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being rich won't protect you from the racism of the rich, and being poor won't protect you from the racism of the poor.<br /> <br /> What's different about Nexus is that the locals are going to have a slightly higher tolerance for weirdness than, say, the people of the Imperial City; they won't freak out and think you're a subhuman monster come to eat their children, but they'll still assume that you are a barbarian, or sneaky, or violent, or (stereotype).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nexus is the second most cosmopolitan city in Creation (right after Great Forks and even then certain beings like demon-blooded can find more acceptance in Nexus than in Great Forks). Ultimately the discrimination a beastman faces there is not going to be nearly as bad as what he or she would face elsewhere. The biggest factor about Nexus is that, if you have money, regardless of what you look like or where you come from, people will be willing to deal with you and you'll find some level of acceptance. <br /> <br /> A wealthy beastman probably isn't going to find any major metropolitan areas in Creation more willing to accept him and treat him as an equal than Nexus. And a destitute beastman in Nexus isn't really going to be all that much worse off than all of the other poor people starving to death. So while a beastman in Nexus may face discrimination, it's important to keep in mind that the core of that discrimination is based around how much money he has. If he had more money, he would be treated better, and he if had less money, he would be treated worse. In many other parts of Creation, a wealthy beastman would be seen as no different than a poor one - just another monster that poses a danger to humans. <br /> <br /> And it's important to remember that this core idea, that Nexus experiences a type economic discrimination and that it applies equally for <i>everyone</i> in Nexus. Any person with money in Nexus will be treated fairly well, regardless of their race, creed or nationality, and anyone without money is going to be treated like trash. Whether you're Imperial or Lookshayan, whether you're mortal or demonblooded, beastman or Anathema, how you're treated is nearly always going to come down to how much money you have. <br /> <br /> That's not to say that beastmen won't face discrimination in Nexus, just that the discrimination they do face is primarily going to be a bit different from what they would face in other parts of Creation, and will ultimately be determined by their economic standing rather than simply because of the fact that they don't look human. And when they do experience discrimination because of their features, it's going to be rather less than what they would have experienced almost anywhere else in Creation.<br /> <br /> So a beastman in a Nexus bar might find that the service for him is slower than other people... though if he obviously had money to spend, he'd find that his order was brought to him first, before anyone else in the bar. Money is the most important factor and the great equalizer in Nexus and tends to trump anything else. So a wealthy beastman would be accepted and a poor one would be rejected - but that is equally true for regular humans too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T15:53:12-07:00","id":680451,"title":"","content":"It's perfectly possible that someone who sees a beastman walking through Nexus thinks &quot;probably a beggar or a slave&quot;. If he's wearing fancy clothes, &quot;probably a slave of someone who likes to have even his (exotic) slaves well-dressed to leave an impact&quot;. There are probably enough ways to magically enforce servitude that a wealthy person who likes to have his slaves look fancy can afford to have them walk around without obvious chains.<br /> <br /> Only once it becomes clear that no, the beastmen has money which is actually his own, that reaction is obviously going to change, but it's still discrimination, because the first reaction is &quot;There's no way he himself could own real money&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> And <i>then</i> there's the possibility where some people might have to pay more than other people because they're considered untrustworthy, and thus fewer are willing to deal with them, allowing those who are willing to demand higher prices.<br /> I mean, if you're dealing with Fair Folk, you're hopefully adding on some risk tax. Some will refuse dealing with them at all because they don't want their soul eaten, and the lower competition means those willing to take that risk can demand higher prices.<br /> Beastmen are similar, though not as dangerous as Fair Folk - but also less able to screw with you if they're offended by your prices, so feel free to demand offensive prices (just keep them less offensive than your competition).<br /> <br /> <br /> You can get nearly everything in Nexus, for the right price. Doesn't mean that the &quot;right price&quot; is the same for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T17:12:11-07:00","id":680530,"title":"","content":"I never said that Nexus was a utopian hugbox free from racism<br /> <br /> That would be a silly claim to make because there isn't a single place in the setting that is free of racism. Whether in Chiaroscuro, Yu-Shan or Malfeas, people will always face discrimination for what they look like or what they are. All that I said was that a beastman (with money) would be fully accepted in Nexus - that doesn't mean he would be loved or that people in Nexus don't discriminate, but in Nexus at least, race and appearance are considered much less important than money. Money is considered the most important thing, not what you look like, not what religion you follow, not where you were born or what language you speak.<br /> <br /> If you have enough money, even if you look like some kind of monster, you'll still be able to find people willing to deal with you in Nexus, which definitely won't be the case in many other major metropolitan cities in Creation like the Imperial City or Azure, where a beastman would be lucky to be allowed to walk the streets in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-27-2015, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T17:58:27-07:00","id":680562,"title":"","content":"A super wealthy beastperson in Nexus probably lives in whatever mansion they can be safe and comfortable in and has servants who deal with the outside world.<br /> <br /> TBH? if I had an npc that lived in nexus and was rich and looked like<a href=\"http://pathfinder-rpg.wdfiles.com/local--files/race:charr/charr1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> this</a>, I'd have him set up with the appearance of being someone's enforcer. Whoever that someone is would be my mouthpiece and everyone would think I'm just their exotic bodyguard. It would probably end up a more interesting story, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T19:35:34-07:00","id":680602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/675454-outcaste-dragonblooded-beastmen?p=679475#post679475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, because there are no artifacts, hearthstones and strange magics that an &quot;enemy of Creation&quot; might use to make their anima appear like that of the dragon-blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but such things would be pretty damn hard to find, especially during the Wyld Hunt's Heyday when there were about a dozen solars spread across Creation instead of 150. It's an outlier. You get those every now and then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://fo